[[:db/retract 17592186192763 :question/answer-fields 17592186189427] {:db/id "q-100493/selection/ma-v1/cd1d051d7b57197ba874ff777b54dd0c909fd7cb4a9f65d23e915c3e0a265657/07a3540ad51bfb53d362c69b0c3835b387a5d7d769d089dc5189f608ec57d640" :answer/id #uuid "0a2c73e3-12c2-54e0-accd-075acdefb760" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100493/selection/ma-v1/cd1d051d7b57197ba874ff777b54dd0c909fd7cb4a9f65d23e915c3e0a265657/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" :answer/id #uuid "83bd4dc4-15ed-56c5-83cf-cbdfe0df5ecb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The integral diverges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100493/selection/ma-v1/cd1d051d7b57197ba874ff777b54dd0c909fd7cb4a9f65d23e915c3e0a265657/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "cc5ce050-0937-5f3e-bbc3-193b25e16d0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100493/selection/ma-v1/cd1d051d7b57197ba874ff777b54dd0c909fd7cb4a9f65d23e915c3e0a265657/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" :answer/id #uuid "c29789e4-0bee-5616-9707-d9cff0341028" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100493/selection/ma-v1/cd1d051d7b57197ba874ff777b54dd0c909fd7cb4a9f65d23e915c3e0a265657/1e940709a1b00fa910544fd0093551b452ea4b241ad5d9959525312e8a27fa19" :answer/id #uuid "2b99bfa8-e91a-5282-877a-f4ee9f1a97f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100493/selection/ma-v1/cd1d051d7b57197ba874ff777b54dd0c909fd7cb4a9f65d23e915c3e0a265657" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f789aa0-2fc0-52d1-ac9f-5781bc2e56c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-100493/selection/ma-v1/cd1d051d7b57197ba874ff777b54dd0c909fd7cb4a9f65d23e915c3e0a265657/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" :answer-field/choices ["q-100493/selection/ma-v1/cd1d051d7b57197ba874ff777b54dd0c909fd7cb4a9f65d23e915c3e0a265657/07a3540ad51bfb53d362c69b0c3835b387a5d7d769d089dc5189f608ec57d640" "q-100493/selection/ma-v1/cd1d051d7b57197ba874ff777b54dd0c909fd7cb4a9f65d23e915c3e0a265657/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" "q-100493/selection/ma-v1/cd1d051d7b57197ba874ff777b54dd0c909fd7cb4a9f65d23e915c3e0a265657/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-100493/selection/ma-v1/cd1d051d7b57197ba874ff777b54dd0c909fd7cb4a9f65d23e915c3e0a265657/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" "q-100493/selection/ma-v1/cd1d051d7b57197ba874ff777b54dd0c909fd7cb4a9f65d23e915c3e0a265657/1e940709a1b00fa910544fd0093551b452ea4b241ad5d9959525312e8a27fa19"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-100493"] :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\sqrt{3}/6}\\frac{1}{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+(kx)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(kx)+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\sqrt{3}/6}\\frac{1}{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{\\sqrt{3}/6}\\frac{1}{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{\\sqrt{3}/6}\\frac{1}{1+(2t)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2t)]}_{a}^{\\sqrt{3}/6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2a)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2a)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)]=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)]=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052212/assets/4612e37c6c611cbaa44c09f4dcc47d006ad45403fff9af5b4df7dca71693dd6e.png)\n\n \n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\sqrt{3}/6}\\frac{1}{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2a)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-100493/selection/ma-v1/cd1d051d7b57197ba874ff777b54dd0c909fd7cb4a9f65d23e915c3e0a265657"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-152641/selection/1e940709a1b00fa910544fd0093551b452ea4b241ad5d9959525312e8a27fa19" :answer/id #uuid "da01d72b-39c2-5784-8d83-98a552b568ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152641/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "e516812a-9ceb-539d-a93b-688435a1b10e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152641/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "3f05526f-9f8b-56ce-beb8-69ba6a182ca8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152641/selection/4499d8f19d109b1dcbb9aed0038cd5542b1326a2018a69856532b0d2aff9810e" :answer/id #uuid "9e157e4c-6465-5adf-813d-648ba5830a7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152641/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" :answer/id #uuid "a1675bc8-d54e-574a-a989-c969c619f103" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The integral diverges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152641/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a0bab367-668d-5922-92ae-db8a6ac76211" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-152641/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer-field/choices ["q-152641/selection/1e940709a1b00fa910544fd0093551b452ea4b241ad5d9959525312e8a27fa19" "q-152641/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-152641/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" "q-152641/selection/4499d8f19d109b1dcbb9aed0038cd5542b1326a2018a69856532b0d2aff9810e" "q-152641/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-152641" :question/id #uuid "8a604ae5-8ec7-51cb-9382-edcd4c89b8e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-152641" :question/problem "Use the substitution $u=\\sqrt{x}$ to evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we substitute $u=\\sqrt{x}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,⟹\\,2\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $x\\to \\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=\\sqrt{x}$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(u)]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)] \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)]-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)]=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)]=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052212/assets/46e6cf2950c99831a7445a862fb36a6a7b8f9233a82e49c7cf5da4a383ec4756.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)]-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-152641/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "808894a0-c611-5eb7-bd57-7f7029f0ef0c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-152641"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-152663/selection/1799e19c9a3a0d0b1889be2c54ab73f5730109da85155b3b8b0ccf6c4adbeaca" :answer/id #uuid "66c7e862-6117-5fa7-ac72-91ae179ca107" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152663/selection/6574705814da0db6b3aa28dbb2a09d324bd280d2223ca9aa9dd5784f9d06bd93" :answer/id #uuid "690440be-f2ae-556f-9d0a-6399b4428f5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152663/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" :answer/id #uuid "a096eaa1-769b-5eb0-a14e-e534281f0e56" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The integral diverges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152663/selection/d62732e72e17b0393290bd9e548ef368f6b7424bded817d038b07db5bf5fcb98" :answer/id #uuid "41e79f64-6c98-5141-bcbd-52d5aa03e3a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152663/selection/8a1510178a4cef63563a4ac588750516c9ef48f71042305065b592e251ef901b" :answer/id #uuid "f7cf84ad-a41c-5ebe-bff0-adedd4497ef6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152663/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cf3e22f9-d133-5230-909c-8a8f2d573796" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-152663/selection/1799e19c9a3a0d0b1889be2c54ab73f5730109da85155b3b8b0ccf6c4adbeaca" :answer-field/choices ["q-152663/selection/1799e19c9a3a0d0b1889be2c54ab73f5730109da85155b3b8b0ccf6c4adbeaca" "q-152663/selection/6574705814da0db6b3aa28dbb2a09d324bd280d2223ca9aa9dd5784f9d06bd93" "q-152663/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" "q-152663/selection/d62732e72e17b0393290bd9e548ef368f6b7424bded817d038b07db5bf5fcb98" "q-152663/selection/8a1510178a4cef63563a4ac588750516c9ef48f71042305065b592e251ef901b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-152663" :question/id #uuid "053bd59b-4b2a-56b6-a74f-9340e9748010" :question/math-academy-id "q-152663" :question/problem "Use the substitution $u={t}^{3}$ to evaluate ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{1+25{t}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we substitute $u={t}^{3}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=3{t}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3{t}^{2}\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to -\\infty $ when $t\\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={t}^{3}$ is as follows:\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $-\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $-\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{1+25{t}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{1}{1+25{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{1+25{t}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{1}{1+25{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{1}{1+25{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5u)]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5u)]_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5a)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5a)]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x)]=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x)]=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052212/assets/06f99111a041ff564ece3019e7dba5331bb4f225d224dff07bb92d83f4e33eb2.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{1+25{t}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}t & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5a)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-152663/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "808894a0-c611-5eb7-bd57-7f7029f0ef0c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-152663"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351570/field-1/473f36def7c891a510b40fec288aebb8efc7d39229fe13e1cfe822cc74e4d9ff" :answer/id #uuid "7111d14f-4cea-5273-975f-a5fb19e721fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8\\pi}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351570/field-1/52c87b0a682a19340b4e6e7cfe0374d7d2f0e6ecf0887e855bd23921720e9acc" :answer/id #uuid "57555404-8293-5cca-aaa2-f8bc2e587b5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4\\pi}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351570/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "edca3d9a-6e67-574a-bf14-4a747126ce77" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351570/field-1/473f36def7c891a510b40fec288aebb8efc7d39229fe13e1cfe822cc74e4d9ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-351570/field-1/473f36def7c891a510b40fec288aebb8efc7d39229fe13e1cfe822cc74e4d9ff" "q-351570/field-1/52c87b0a682a19340b4e6e7cfe0374d7d2f0e6ecf0887e855bd23921720e9acc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351570" :question/id #uuid "3086a253-c86d-55f4-a355-82e7388716fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-351570" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{12}{{x}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{k}^{2}+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{k})+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{12}{{x}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}x & =12\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})]}_{a}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{3})) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{6}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{3})).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052212/assets/24ca4823d220c3eb31127ed28ab7c75b1297e10ae20a1926d112a234806c411e.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{12}{{x}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{6}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{3})) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{2\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-351570/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8a8bf54-5523-5eaa-a236-b8931d1c3dba"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351570"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351573/field-1/9e199bee4b6bbf53d3151b37709f328f258ed52259df9c2193b9064913d640cc" :answer/id #uuid "65bed312-8452-55b3-947b-9b80a311307f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351573/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1fa79485-3dde-506d-89cf-179d9510a873" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351573/field-1/9e199bee4b6bbf53d3151b37709f328f258ed52259df9c2193b9064913d640cc" :answer-field/choices ["q-351573/field-1/9e199bee4b6bbf53d3151b37709f328f258ed52259df9c2193b9064913d640cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351573" :question/id #uuid "8e56c7bf-d5d0-5771-b448-7fa309825fc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-351573" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{5}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+25}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{k}^{2}+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{k})+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{5}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+25}\\,\\text{d}x & =6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{5}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+25}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{5}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{5}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})]}_{a}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{5})) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{4}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{5})).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{5}),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052212/assets/f8325b1ea152bd40aaa909202bfce59e621952486041c657c0e27b9192ecec03.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{5}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+25}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{6}{5}\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{4}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{5})) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{4}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-351573/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8a8bf54-5523-5eaa-a236-b8931d1c3dba"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351573"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
